Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 01:55:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] correlation groups: min_coherence; converged rank-1 fit;
 merge-back by correlation affinity

- A significant group whose coherence is at least min_coherence (default 0.03, correlation
  units) is reported even when the population it is separated from has strong internal
  structure (separation_ratio alone misses a group next to a structured majority).
- rank1_fit: damped update (the simultaneous update oscillated when reliabilities differ
  widely and stopped short of convergence).
- A rejected candidate goes back to the population it correlates with as well as that
  population's members correlate with each other (residuals sent half of a continuously
  varying majority to a minority pair).
- Tests at realistic within-population variation; tests for min_coherence and the merge-back.
---
